        <mxCell id="pdretrievedlbl" value="green border = retrieved as relevant" style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;fontSize=10;fontColor=#82b366;fontStyle=2;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1080" y="844" width="240" height="32" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="pdprocon" value="&lt;b&gt;Pro:&lt;/b&gt;  scales to arbitrarily long histories. Tokens per call stay tiny no matter how many past turns exist.&#xa;&lt;b&gt;Con:&lt;/b&gt;  retrieval can miss subtle context (e.g. tone, the running joke from 50 turns ago, or an instruction the user gave once that should always apply). Often paired with a small recent-window so you do not lose continuity for the last few turns. Common in long-running personal assistants and customer support bots." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;fontSize=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=10;" vertex="1" parent="1">
